From a82dff1dc6bb3bf15dc1b245c74e7b9be24b6c1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azra Bano <azrabano.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:36:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BUG: Do not report poolability F-test with robust covariance

The poolability F-test in PanelOLS is computed from residual sums of
squares and is only valid under homoskedasticity, yet it was reported
unchanged when a robust, clustered or kernel covariance was used. Return
an InvalidTestStatistic in these cases, which matches Stata where F_f is
only reported for vce(conventional). Also fix the remaining reference to
the 'cluster' weight type in the IV docs, which should be 'clustered'.

xref #631
